From: custom
Subject: [PATCH] mt7981 cudy tr3000 256mb: drop the hard-coded mtd-layout cmdline

0004 gave the "default" layout a cmdline of its own:

    cmdline = "console=ttyS0,115200n1 loglevel=8 ubi.mtd=ubi";

board_mtdparts_default() exports that through the `bootargs` environment
variable, and fdt_chosen() *replaces* the FIT's /chosen/bootargs wholesale
whenever that variable is non-empty. So the command line the factory image
carries about itself got thrown away.

Dumping the factory bootloader and the factory image says that is the wrong
direction. The factory FIP contains no `console=`, no `earlycon` and no
`bootargs=` string at all; its only mtd-related literal is a built-in

    nmbm0:1024k(bl2),512k(u-boot-env),2048k(factory),256k(bdinfo),2048k(fip),235520k(ubi)

The factory kernel FIT in the UBI carries

    console=ttyS0,115200n1 loglevel=8 earlycon=uart8250,mmio32,0x11002000

in /chosen/bootargs, and the UBI volume table is the usual
kernel / rootfs / rootfs_data. The factory image therefore boots off its own
command line, with no bootargs variable in the environment at all, and none
of the ubi.rootfs_volume / boot_param.* entries 0002 used to add are needed.

Let the layout set no cmdline. cmdline stays NULL, board_mtdparts_default()
clears the variable, board_fdt_chosen_bootargs() returns NULL, fdt_chosen()
leaves the FIT's /chosen/bootargs alone -- byte-for-byte the factory
behaviour. `vendor_bootargs` (0004) is still there for anyone who wants to
override the command line from the prompt.

Requires 0001 .. 0004.

Apply with:
    git apply 0005-uboot-multi-layout-no-cmdline.patch
Fallback if your tree normalises EOLs differently:
    git apply --ignore-whitespace 0005-uboot-multi-layout-no-cmdline.patch
    patch -p1 -l < 0005-uboot-multi-layout-no-cmdline.patch

---
diff --git a/uboot-mtk-20250711/arch/arm/dts/mt7981-cudy-tr3000-v1-256mb.dts b/uboot-mtk-20250711/arch/arm/dts/mt7981-cudy-tr3000-v1-256mb.dts
index 95c4752..f91c170 100644
--- a/uboot-mtk-20250711/arch/arm/dts/mt7981-cudy-tr3000-v1-256mb.dts
+++ b/uboot-mtk-20250711/arch/arm/dts/mt7981-cudy-tr3000-v1-256mb.dts
@@ -25,39 +25,51 @@
 	/*
 	 * Two partition maps for one board, selected at run time through the
 	 * `mtd_layout_label` environment variable (web UI: 高级功能 -> MTD 布局).
-	 *
-	 * The first five partitions are identical in both, so BL2 and the FIP
-	 * never move: only the size of the UBI partition changes. Nothing in
+	 * The first five partitions are identical in both maps, so BL2 and the FIP
+	 * never move: only the size of the UBI partition changes, and nothing in
 	 * the boot chain outside U-Boot has to know which map is active.
+	 *
+	 * Neither map sets `cmdline`, and that is deliberate.
+	 *
+	 * The factory bootloader installs *no* `bootargs` variable at all -- the
+	 * only mtd-related string in its FIP is an explicit
+	 *     nmbm0:1024k(bl2),512k(u-boot-env),2048k(factory),256k(bdinfo),
+	 *           2048k(fip),235520k(ubi)
+	 * -- and the factory kernel is started with nothing but the
+	 * /chosen/bootargs its own FIT carries:
+	 *     console=ttyS0,115200n1 loglevel=8 earlycon=uart8250,mmio32,0x11002000
+	 * (the FIT also spells the UBI volume names out: kernel / rootfs /
+	 * rootfs_data). Whatever was appended on top of that -- ubi.rootfs_volume,
+	 * the boot_param.* set -- is not needed to boot the factory image.
+	 *
+	 * board_mtdparts_default() clears the `bootargs` variable when the active
+	 * layout has no `cmdline` property, and fdt_chosen() then leaves the FIT's
+	 * own /chosen/bootargs untouched, so this reproduces the factory behaviour
+	 * exactly.
+	 *
+	 * If a command line is wanted after all, set `vendor_bootargs`: the vendor
+	 * boot path replaces `bootargs` with it verbatim, one setenv and no
+	 * rebuild.
 	 */
 	mtd-layout {
 		/*
-		 * layout@0 -- Cudy factory layout.
-		 *
-		 * Byte for byte the map the stock bootloader hands to the stock
-		 * firmware, so an image written by this U-Boot boots with exactly
-		 * the partitioning it was built for, and UBI keeps the size it
-		 * already has on the flash.
+		 * layout@0 -- the factory map, and the map the OpenWrt /
+		 * ImmortalWrt images for this board are built against.
 		 *
-		 * The stock images carry only their console settings in
-		 * /chosen/bootargs -- everything else used to live in the factory
-		 * environment, which does not survive another firmware writing the
-		 * env partition. Supply it here instead. `ubi.mtd` is what makes
-		 * the kernel attach the UBI device; the rootfs volume itself is
-		 * resolved by the kernel's own default rootdev logic, so there is
-		 * deliberately no `root=`.
+		 * `-(ubi)` expands to "everything the NMBM device has left", which
+		 * is the 235520 KiB the factory mtdparts string spells out
+		 * explicitly.
 		 */
 		layout@0 {
 			label = "default";
 			mtdids = "nmbm0=nmbm0";
 			mtdparts = "nmbm0:1024k(bl2),512k(u-boot-env),2048k(Factory),256k(bdinfo),2048k(fip),-(ubi)";
-			cmdline = "console=ttyS0,115200n1 loglevel=8 ubi.mtd=ubi";
 		};
 
 		/*
-		 * layout@1 -- 112 MiB UBI, the layout the ubootmod / 112m-nmbm
-		 * images for this board expect. Those bring a complete command
-		 * line of their own, so none is set here.
+		 * layout@1 -- 112 MiB UBI, for images built against the 112m-nmbm
+		 * map. Smaller than the factory UBI, so switching to it never moves
+		 * anything below it.
 		 */
 		layout@1 {
 			label = "112m";
